# Caddyfile — TLS termination + path-based routing to the one engine
# instance. Caddy proxies WebSocket upgrades transparently (no special
# config needed beyond a normal reverse_proxy), so `/ws` just works.
#
# Site address comes from $DOMAIN (.env, read via docker-compose's
# `env_file` on the caddy service — see docker-compose.prod.yml):
#   - Have a domain pointed at this VPS's IP (an A record)? Set
#     DOMAIN=realtime.example.com in .env — Caddy gets you a real,
#     auto-renewing Let's Encrypt certificate for it automatically, no
#     extra config. Do this once DNS has propagated
#     (`dig +short your-domain` should print the VPS's IP).
#   - No domain yet, IP only? Set DOMAIN=:80 — Caddy then serves plain
#     HTTP on port 80 (no certificate to issue for a bare IP). Switch to
#     the domain form the moment you have one and restart Caddy
#     (`docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml restart caddy`).

{$DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy /ws* service-messengio:8080
	reverse_proxy /api/* service-messengio:8090
}
